WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Dedicated normal reviewer confirmed. This is a live verification view of native MCP calls, not the Dots conversation UI.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:14.000
The actual fighter.json reached the cloud MCP through the host file input. Eleven WebP assets were requested.

3
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:20.000
First real WebP uploaded. The service verified its bytes and SHA-256 against the manifest.

4
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Walk, run and fight-idle uploads succeeded. Existing approved artwork is unchanged.

5
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Eight of eleven actual files uploaded, including attacks and block. No new artwork was generated.

6
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:39.000
All eleven files, 5,537,184 bytes, passed upload verification. Uploading alone is not registration.

7
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:47.000
The explicit registration request returned queued. The video condenses the wait for the server worker.

8
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:54.000
The server returned registered, with all eleven assets validated and runtimeApproved true.

9
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:02.000
The new fighter appears in the reviewer-owned list. The registered immutable manifest hash matches the submitted file.

